ies going through their very personal cremation ceremonies, as well as a fair amount of physical and psychological unease at breathing in smoke containing human ashes, my visit to Pashupatinath was totally worthwhile.  Not just the ceremony, but the architecture, the colours, the intense characters I photographed...well worth going.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 37, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "solo", "stay_date": "2012-09-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "D973F59DC1021E5BFB374607C2F90296", "name": "Deanno", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/Deanno", "username": "Deanno", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-s/01/ba/27/fb/deanno.jpg", "contribution_count": 141, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2012-10-05", "published_at_date": "2012-10-05"}, {"review_id": 141984963, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r141984963-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "An eye opener!", "text": "This is in-your-face Kathmandu at its best. But you must have a stomach for burning bodies and transient sadhus etc. This is a place to see but probably not to linger. Note that not all of this site is open to non-Hindus.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 2, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "friends", "stay_date": "2012-09-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "23A8AFFCF5F0352ED369096DF98ADCB2", "name": "dr_iggy", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/dr_iggy", "username": "dr_iggy", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-s/02/8a/92/82/dr-iggy.jpg", "contribution_count": 454, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2012-10-04", "published_at_date": "2012-10-04"}, {"review_id": 141969605, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r141969605-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Pashupatinath Temple", "text": "Interesting , Funny though it may sound walking in I actually saw a few monkeys mimicing the humans and were going round the shivling in silence heads bent ! Unfortunately as I tried to take a oic they ran off !\n", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 2, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "family", "stay_date": "2012-09-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "9C09E74C22135481AAF576532A201B12", "name": "DeepaNebb", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/DeepaNebb", "username": "DeepaNebb", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/05/5d/e1/1a/deepanebb.jpg", "contribution_count": 68, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2012-10-04", "published_at_date": "2012-10-04"}, {"review_id": 141961252, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r141961252-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Tranquil", "text": "Pashupati is a beautiful old set of temples and the current spot for cremations--Its a little strange watching cremations just across the river--seeing full bodies--but its still a serene atmosphere--if you go up into Pashupati, atop the hill--you'll get great views and see old sadu babas (drifting holy men) hanging out, smoking chillum, and drinking chai.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "solo", "stay_date": "2012-10-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "F619ACE96259589B8A80F61DBEC17083", "name": "mira m", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/miram756", "username": "miram756", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/e9/60/default-avatar-2020-64.jpg", "contribution_count": 12, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 293890, "location_name": "Kathmandu", "location_name_detailed": "Kathmandu, Nepal"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2012-10-04", "published_at_date": "2012-10-03"}, {"review_id": 141130890, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r141130890-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Not exactly a place for people who has a low tolerance level of human cremation", "text": "It is indeed a sad place, this is where they cremate dead hindus, they do it by the river bank. Be aware of taking picture as some consider it offensive. Just cross the bridge to the opposite side, look for a nice place to sit, and zoom all the way your camera and take a quick snap. Monkeys are everywhere, be careful with your cams or bottled water, they might just snatch it.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 3, "subratings": [], "like_count": 2, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": null, "stay_date": null}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "4041AC8983479121892D6ADA7110D8D4", "name": "mockamore", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/mockamore", "username": "mockamore", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-s/03/06/35/82/mockamore.jpg", "contribution_count": 4, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2012-09-24", "published_at_date": "2012-09-24"}, {"review_id": 141107179, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r141107179-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Ancient and Eternal", "text": "Although foreigners are not allowed into the main temples, one can explore the extensive temple grounds. There is a feeling of sanctity that permeates the whole environment. It's easy to forget that you are surrounded by a city of almost 5 million people. The noise and pollution fall away and you can enjoy the feeling of peacefulness. I can see why it has been considered a special and holy site for many generations.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 1, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "friends", "stay_date": "2012-09-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "7E2F9155BD0449F88603257061F6712A", "name": "MARKOLA111", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/MARKOLA111", "username": "MARKOLA111", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/e2/e6/default-avatar-2020-45.jpg", "contribution_count": 76, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 60878, "location_name": "Seattle", "location_name_detailed": "Seattle, Washington"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2012-09-24", "published_at_date": "2012-09-24"}, {"review_id": 140904950, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r140904950-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "No worth to pay fee 500 Rs", "text": "Becouse you are not allowed to enter inside of the temple dont pay the fee of 500 rs. when we went to the ghat nobody ask the payment so i guees its free.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 3, "subratings": [], "like_count": 1, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "couples", "stay_date": "2012-09-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "6ABE8ECB9FB86461252CDD0E4C38C6EF", "name": "tomjorss", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/tomjorss", "username": "tom